          "type": "turn",
          "question": "How often does guidance describe checking thyroid function once treatment is stable?",
          "answer": "According to guidance from the Endocrinology and Thyroid Association, thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) levels are rechecked six to eight weeks after starting levothyroxine or after any change in dose. This interval allows the body to re-equilibrate to the new steady state of the medication (guideline-hypothyroidism-testing-and-monitoring).\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
